{
    "article_summary": "This article explores the first use of multi-resonant thermally activated delayed fluorescent (MR-TADF) compounds, specifically DiKTa and Mes3DiKTa, as organic photocatalysts. The study demonstrates that these rigid nanographene derivatives perform comparably or superiorly to the benchmark donor-acceptor TADF catalyst 4CzIPN across a variety of reactions including reductive quenching (photo-Giese), oxidative quenching (ATRA), energy transfer (isomerization), and dual catalysis (Ni-catalyzed cross-coupling and HAT-mediated deiodination). Key findings include enhanced reaction rates and effectiveness at lower catalyst loadings due to high molar absorptivity and triplet energies.",
